WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.830
When the Fed acts, the headlines
all say the same thing:

2
00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:05.540
interest rates are going up,

3
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.100
or coming down.

4
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.450
But an interest rate is a price.

5
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.630
It's the price of holding
money instead of bonds.

6
00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.930
Cash in your wallet earns nothing.

7
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.850
That lost interest is
the cost of keeping it.

8
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.620
So if money has a price,

9
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.240
what makes that price go up or down?

10
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.010
In this mission, you'll
draw the money market graph,

11
00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.810
with every curve and label in its place.

12
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.620
Then you'll change the
price level in a graph lab,

13
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.220
predict the new interest rate,

14
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.600
and check. Your mission: find out
what moves the price of money.
